  "note": "Each relay n coil is fed at nF with nC on the minus rail (1C..6C chain, 6C/6-), so its indicator lamp is in series with the coil. Each relay latches through its own set-1 N.O. contact fed from the relay above it (6H on plus, 6G=5H, 5G=4H, ..., 2G=1H). Pushbutton k with slide switch k LEFT feeds the next relay down through the set-2 N.O. chain (pushbutton 1 calls relay 6 at 6com/6F; pushbutton 2 calls relay 5 through 6L/6K; ... pushbutton 6 calls relay 1 through 2L/2K). Light 1 is wired 1A/1G and 1B/1-, and 1F/1G ties 1G to the feed end of relay 1's coil, so light 1 lights only when relay 1 is called, after all twelve steps. The page states one observable: light 1 \"will come on\" when all twelve steps are completed. It is asserted OFF after step 11 (just before pushbutton 6 is pushed) and ON after step 12. Per-step relay and indicator-lamp states are not printed and are left to Step 7. 'If you attempt to carry out a step in the wrong order, nothing will happen' names no observable, so it is not asserted. The printed reset (all slide switches RIGHT, power off, then on) is scripted but states no observable.",
